und:#141b2d;border-radius:8px;padding:14px;\"\u003e\u003cdiv style=\"font-size:11px;font-weight:600;color:#fbbf24;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.5px;margin-bottom:6px;\"\u003eRates and Energy\u003c/div\u003e\u003cp style=\"margin:0;font-size:13px;color:#e2e8f0;line-height:1.6;\"\u003eThe 4.78% 10Y and WTI near 92.96 remain the main cross-asset checkpoints. EIA petroleum inventories are delayed to Thursday at noon ET after Labor Day, with natural gas at 10:30 AM ET.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style=\"background:#1a1f2e;border:1px solid #2d3748;border-radius:12px;padding:20px;margin-bottom:20px;\"\u003e\u003cdiv style=\"font-size:11px;font-weight:600;color:#94a3b8;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.6px;margin-bottom:14px;\"\u003eOmissions and Watch\u003c/div\u003e\u003cp style=\"margin:0 0 10px;font-size:13px;color:#e2e8f0;line-height:1.7;\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eOmitted today:\u003c/strong\u003e BLS calendar access returned HTTP 403, so no BLS release was inferred. BEA shows no release for 2026-09-08; EIA has no same-day inventory release; NAR was not required for today\u0027s verified calendar.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp style=\"margin:0;font-size:13px;color:#e2e8f0;line-height:1.7;\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWatch:\u003c/strong\u003e TreasuryDirect confirms 17-week Bill on 2026-09-09 and 4-week, 8-week, 13-week and 26-week Bills on 2026-09-10, but their exact closing times were not included in the dated source set used here. They remain watch items, not selected calendar rows.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style=\"background:#1a1f2e;border:1px solid #2d3748;border-radius:12px;padding:20px;margin-bottom:20px;\"\u003e\u003cdiv style=\"font-size:11px;font-weight:600;color:#94a3b8;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.6px;margin-bottom:14px;\"\u003eTrading Strategy Note - ES Futures\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(240px,1fr));gap:14px;\"\u003e\u003cdiv style=\"background:#141b2d;border-radius:8px;padding:14px;border-left:3px solid #34d399;\"\u003e\u003cdiv style=\"font-size:11px;font-weight:600;color:#34d399;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.5px;margin-bottom:8px;\"\u003eBase Case\u003c/div\u003e\u003cp style=\"margin:0;font-size:13px;color:#e2e8f0;line-height:1.6;\"\u003eES is 7723.25 overnight, but the 10:00 AM Census release and 11:00 AM to 1:00 PM Treasury auction cluster create event risk. Negative NFCI, SOFR at 3.66%, and MOVE below 80 support a measured constructive bias, while WTI near 92.96 argues against chasing strength.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv style=\"background:#141b2d;border-radius:8px;padding:14px;border-left:3px solid #f87171;\"\u003e\u003cdiv style=\"font-size:11px;font-weight:600;color:#f87171;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.5px;margin-bottom:8px;\"\u003eInvalidation\u003c/div\u003e\u003cp style=\"margin:0;font-size:13px;color:#e2e8f0;line-height:1.6;\"\u003eLose 7700 and hold below it, or see 10Y above 4.85% and MOVE back above 80, and the constructive bias is invalidated. A weak Treasury auction, a hawkish H.10 reaction, or a sharp oil gap also invalidates continuation assumptions.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/div\u003e"}